amily_name: null, models: 29 entries.\n\nOrder: DN40, DN50, DN65, DN80, DN100, DN125, DN150, DN200, DN250, DN300, DN350, DN400, DN450, DN500, DN600, DN700, DN750, DN800, DN900, DN1000, DN1050, DN1100, DN1200, DN1350, DN1400, DN1500, DN1600, DN1650, DN1800.\n\ncharacteristics:\ntype_level:\n- ratio_q2_q1: {value: 1.6, unit_symbol: null}\n- ratio_q4_q3: {value: 1.25, unit_symbol: null}\n- minimum_ratio_q3_q1: {value: 40, unit_symbol: null}\n\nmodel_level:\n- permanent_flow_rate_q3: unit m³/h, values per 29 models.\n- overload_flow_rate_q4: unit m³/h, values per 29 models.\n\nWait — check Q3 by size across both tables: DN900 mains: Q3=10000 (both classes); battery: 10000. ✓. DN1800: only in table 1: 16000. ✓. DN1600, DN1650: mains 16000, battery 16000 ✓.\n\nQ4 by size: DN900: 12500 both ✓. DN1800: 20000 ✓.\n\nAlso could add model_level accuracy_class? Skip.\n\nShould I include q1_min/q2 per model? They vary with class & power — skip, matrix tables carry them.\n\nmatrix_tables:\n\nTable 1:\n{\n  \"name\": null,\n  \"description\": \"General characteristics of the family of instruments, full bore (table continued from the previous page; its heading is not contained in this fragment). The flow rates Q1 and Q2 are minimum values with Q2/Q1 = 1.6; Q3 and Q4 are maximum values with Q4/Q3 = 1.25; Q3 and ratio Q3/Q1 are selected from paragraph 4.1 of OIML R49-1:2013; ratio Q3/Q1 is at least 40.\",\n  \"columns\": [\"meter_size\", \"accuracy_class\", \"minimum_flow_rate_q1\", \"transitional_flow_rate_q2\", \"permanent_flow_rate_q3\", \"overload_flow_rate_q4\", \"ratio_q3_q1\"],\n  \"column_units\": [null, null, \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", \"m³/h\", null],\n  \"rows\": [...],\n  \"footnotes\": []\n}\n\nHmm, footnotes empty array — fine, or omit. I'll omit footnotes since none.\n\nTable 2:\n{\n  \"name\": \"Table 8 General characteristics of the family of instruments - Full bore - Battery / Renewable energy powered\",\n  ...\n}\n\nActually \"name\" null for table 1 might be odd